<title>PHILIPPINES: Investments in Philippines' economic zones up.</title>
<headline>Investments in Philippines' economic zones up.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investments in the Philippines' economic zones grew 24.36 percent this year to 65.319 billion pesos from last year's 52.524 billion pesos, the Philippine Economic Zone Authority said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Philippines has four regular export processing zones, two duty-free port zones and more than 10 industrial estates.</p>
<p>Investors inside the economic zones enjoy income tax holidays and preferential duties for capital imports.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
